# The network of "Watch the translation", and of every NAT lab: the shop's
# private network behind its gateway, and a small internet.
#
#   office 10.1.0.10 --+                                          +-- srv 203.0.113.10
#                      [shop]-- gw --[isp]-- inet --[internet]----+
#   app 10.1.0.20 -----+   10.1.0.1  198.51.100.2  .1  203.0.113.1 +-- client 203.0.113.20
#
# gw is the shop's gateway, and its forwarding is its own business: its
# /etc/sysctl.d turns it on (netlab's router role would do it for gw, as it
# does for inet). Its firewall is its /etc/nftables.conf, loaded at every
# boot by nftables@gw. inet has no route to 10.0.0.0/8: private addresses
# aren't routed on the internet. gw and inet meet on a switch, isp, the
# provider's network.
machine office
machine app
machine gw
machine inet router
machine srv
machine client

lan shop office:eth0=10.1.0.10/24 app:eth0=10.1.0.20/24 gw:lan=10.1.0.1/24
lan isp gw:wan=198.51.100.2/24 inet:isp=198.51.100.1/24
lan internet inet:pub=203.0.113.1/24 srv:eth0=203.0.113.10/24 client:eth0=203.0.113.20/24

route office default via 10.1.0.1
route app default via 10.1.0.1
route gw default via 198.51.100.1
route srv default via 203.0.113.1
route client default via 203.0.113.1

run gw nftables
run app nginx
run srv nginx
